{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe heat was stifling, but the journey to Bruges has been agreeable enough. I arrived at eight after boarding a canal barge at two. The cabin was pleasantly crowded; passengers read the newspapers or played whist with a fervor that reminded me of our own parlour games. I confess I watched the cards with interest, though I did not join in.\n\nEarlier, in Ghent, I viewed the fragments of the van Eyck altarpiece. The detail is astonishing, a testament to a different kind of spirit. But I find myself thinking less of art and more of the slow, inevitable movement of the state. These canals, these barges, they are not just transport; they are the veins of a commercial order that grows, not as a product of arbitrary will, but as the actuality of the ethical idea.\n\nThe air in Bruges is cooler. I hope this letter finds you and the boys well in Berlin. I miss your company and the quiet of our home.\n\nYours,\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795080621,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":221,"prompt_tokens":937,"total_tokens":1158,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-NWdsQ1u9axNpwwejHhbP3zaYWHaVxlCU","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":937,"prompt_ms":945.885,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.0094823906083243,"prompt_per_second":990.6066805161305,"predicted_n":221,"predicted_ms":5246.817,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.849168181818182,"predicted_per_second":41.930183576061445}}